{%- doc -%}
  Renders the Black Friday offer line for a product: the shopper's saving when
  the variant is discounted, and the shipping offer alone when it is not.

  Rendered inside the section's `Price-{section}-{product}` element on purpose.
  On a variant change theme.js re-fetches the section and swaps only a fixed
  list of regions by id — Price among them, a custom block not. Anywhere else
  the saving would keep the previous variant's figure after a switch, which is
  a wrong discount claim rather than a cosmetic bug.

  The saving is computed exactly as product-price.liquid computes its own
  "Save" figure, down to the currency-code setting and the round, so the two
  numbers on the page can never disagree. Keep them in step.

  Two lines, not one: the benefit carries the weight and the terms sit under it
  muted. A single sentence holding saving, shipping, threshold and deadline ran
  to four lines on a phone directly above the add-to-cart button, where the
  shopper is deciding, and the saving had to be read out of the middle of it.

  CAMPAIGN COPY, ends 30 November 2026. It hides itself after that date, so a
  stale "Ends Monday 30 Nov" cannot outlive the sale, but still delete this
  snippet and its two render tags in main-product.liquid once the sale is over.

  @param {object} product - Product to describe.
  @param {object} [variant] - Variant to price. Defaults to the product's selected or first available.

  @example
  {% render 'black-friday-promo', product: product %}
{%- enddoc -%}

{%- liquid
  assign bf_target = variant | default: product.selected_or_first_available_variant

  comment
    Free shipping is an order-level threshold, in cents to match variant.price.
  endcomment
  assign bf_free_shipping_min = 10000

  comment
    A gift card is not part of a sitewide discount and ships nothing, so
    neither half of the message is true of one.
  endcomment
  assign bf_show = true
  if product.gift_card?
    assign bf_show = false
  endif
  if bf_target == blank
    assign bf_show = false
  endif

  comment
    Self-expire at the end of 30 Nov, Brisbane (UTC+10, no DST). Fails open if
    the date cannot be parsed: showing the offer a little long during the sale
    beats hiding a live offer because of a filter quirk.
  endcomment
  assign bf_now = 'now' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  assign bf_ends = '2026-12-01T00:00:00+10:00' | date: '%s' | plus: 0
  if bf_ends > 0 and bf_now > bf_ends
    assign bf_show = false
  endif
-%}

{%- if bf_show -%}
  {%- liquid
    assign bf_compare_at = bf_target.compare_at_price
    assign bf_price = bf_target.price

    assign bf_on_sale = false
    if bf_compare_at > bf_price
      assign bf_on_sale = true
    endif

    comment
      Where the item alone already clears the threshold, say the shipping is
      included rather than restating a condition the shopper has already met.
      Below it, naming the threshold is both accurate and a reason to add more.
    endcomment
    if bf_price >= bf_free_shipping_min
      assign bf_shipping = 'Free shipping included'
    else
      assign bf_shipping = 'Free shipping on orders over $100'
    endif

    if bf_on_sale
      assign bf_saved_value = bf_compare_at | minus: bf_price
      if settings.currency_code_enabled
        assign bf_saved_money = bf_saved_value | money_with_currency
      else
        assign bf_saved_money = bf_saved_value | money
      endif
      assign bf_saved_pct = bf_saved_value | times: 100.0 | divided_by: bf_compare_at | round
    endif
  -%}
  <div class="bf-promo" style="margin-block-start: var(--sp-2d5);">
    <p
      class="text-sm font-bold leading-tight"
      style="margin: 0; color: rgb(var(--color-success-text));"
    >
      {%- if bf_on_sale -%}
        You&rsquo;re saving {{ bf_saved_money }} ({{ bf_saved_pct }}%) on this item
      {%- else -%}
        {{ bf_shipping }}
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
    <p class="text-opacity text-xs font-medium leading-tight" style="margin: var(--sp-1) 0 0 0;">
      {%- if bf_on_sale -%}
        {{ bf_shipping }} &middot; Black Friday ends Monday 30 Nov
      {%- else -%}
        Black Friday ends Monday 30 Nov
      {%- endif -%}
    </p>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}
